ix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 16 & -11 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 44 & -13 & 16 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -10 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations\n\n- $C_{1}:=C_{1}+5C_{4}$\n- $C_{2}:=\\ldots$\n- $C_{3}:=\\ldots$\n\neach of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{4},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?"] [:db/add "c89ac9d1-a45a-5bb2-8574-f989d9ecbe2b" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries in row 2 other than $a_{24}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 & -6 \\\\ -10 & 4 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}+5C_{4}}\\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 4 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 44 & 3 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -8 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{2}:=C_{2}-2C_{4}}\\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 16 & 7 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 2 \\\\ 44 & -13 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -10 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+3C_{4}}\\begin{bmatrix}-37 & 16 & -11 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 44 & -13 & 16 & 8 \\\\ 11 & -10 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{2}:=C_{2}-2C_{4}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+3C_{4}$."] [:db/add "c89ac9d1-a45a-5bb2-8574-f989d9ecbe2b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "c89ac9d1-a45a-5bb2-8574-f989d9ecbe2b" :question/answer-fields "a5582b1a-5bb6-5cb4-89b2-4fafc470a53b"] [:db/ensure "c89ac9d1-a45a-5bb2-8574-f989d9ecbe2b" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186161966 :knowledge-point/questions "c89ac9d1-a45a-5bb2-8574-f989d9ecbe2b"] [:db/add "f0428e12-0768-579a-a578-078588e9c0f5" :answer/id #uuid "f0428e12-0768-579a-a578-078588e9c0f5"] [:db/add "f0428e12-0768-579a-a578-078588e9c0f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text] [:db/add "f0428e12-0768-579a-a578-078588e9c0f5" :answer/value "$C_{1}:=C_{1